# No Emojis in Code or Documentation

## Rule
**Never use emojis in any files** created or modified in this project. This includes:
- Source code (Python, Lean)
- Documentation (README, CONTRIBUTING, markdown files)
- Comments and docstrings
- Commit messages
- Configuration files
- Any other project files

## Rationale
- Maintains professional, academic tone appropriate for research software
- Ensures compatibility across all text editors and terminals
- Improves readability and reduces visual clutter
- Follows established conventions for formal technical documentation

## Enforcement
- Use plain text lists with hyphens instead of checkmark emojis
- Use descriptive text instead of icon emojis
- Keep all project files emoji-free

## Examples

**Bad:**
```markdown
- ✅ Feature complete
- 🚀 Fast performance
- 🔒 Secure by default
```

**Good:**
```markdown
- Feature complete
- Fast performance
- Secure by default
```
